{"name":"Pink Parade","hex":"#b26ba2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"},{"term":"parade","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An organized display of a group of people, particularly\n Synonym of military parade: A show of troops, an assembly of troops as a show of force, to receive orders, or especially for inspection at set times.\n\nA public procession, especially one commemorating a holiday or special event or  in protest.","Synonym of military parade: A show of troops, an assembly of troops as a show of force, to receive orders, or especially for inspection at set times."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To take part in a parade, particularly:\nTo assemble for inspection, to receive orders, etc.\n\nTo march impressively or ostentatiously.","To assemble for inspection, to receive orders, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parade"}],"entries":[{"title":"Parade","blocks":[{"text":"A parade is a procession of people, usually organized along a street, often in costume, and often accompanied by marching bands, floats, or sometimes large balloons. Parades are held for a wide range of reasons, but are usually some variety of celebration."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Macy%27s_Thanksgiving_Day_Parade_2022_New_York_City_%2852523112564%29.jpg/330px-Macy%27s_Thanksgiving_Day_Parade_2022_New_York_City_%2852523112564%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parade","wikidata":"Q657449"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Federation_Parade%2C_Sydney_032050.jpg/500px-Federation_Parade%2C_Sydney_032050.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Federation_Parade%2C_Sydney_032050.jpg/500px-Federation_Parade%2C_Sydney_032050.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A parade in Sydney to celebrate the Federation of Australia in January 1901","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFederation_Parade%2C_Sydney_032050.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Foundations_for_Our_Future_BYU_parade_float_%2842077328930%29.jpg/500px-Foundations_for_Our_Future_BYU_parade_float_%2842077328930%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Foundations_for_Our_Future_BYU_parade_float_%2842077328930%29.jpg/1280px-Foundations_for_Our_Future_BYU_parade_float_%2842077328930%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Foundations_for_Our_Future_BYU_parade_float_%2842077328930%29.jpg/500px-Foundations_for_Our_Future_BYU_parade_float_%2842077328930%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A parade float for Brigham Young University in the Freedom Festival Grand Parade in 